WEBVTT

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:07.550
Vanguard
National Championship

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.690
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:17.150
It's been a long wait!

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:22.840
But the Vanguard National 
Championship begins right now!

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.950
First off, I'll explain the 
progression of this tournament.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:34.250
To start, the 32 participating teams 
will be divided into eight blocks.

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:35.050
And then...

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.270
Hello, hello! Thank you! Thank you!

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:42.460
E-Excuse me, but this isn't the plan!

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.650
Don't worry about it!

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:47.820
Hi! I'm Rekka from Ultra-rare!

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.190
And I'm Suiko.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:56.650
Hey, hey, Mr. Miya, it works the 
same way as last time, right?

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:58.540
Well, right, but...

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:01.700
Um, on stage, you shouldn't really 
turn your back to the audience.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:09.290
If the rules are the same, I'm sure 
you all remember them, don't you?

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:11.300
Yes!!

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:14.730
There, see?

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:20.900
You wanna skip over the boring explanations 
and get right to the fights, right?!

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:23.460
That's right! That's right!

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:25.310
Get the fights goin'!

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:28.320
What about first things first...?

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:30.130
See? Everyone's fired up!

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:31.930
Th-That's true...

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:35.110
Fine, the heck with the rules!

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:37.820
Let's go to the grouping lottery!

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:38.850
Yeah!!

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:41.110
Hold it!!

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:43.370
W-What is it?

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.120
What about Kourin?!

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.690
Morikawa...

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:49.070
Although you're right...

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:51.160
Oh, sorry.

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:54.090
Kourin is feeling under the weather...

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:58.000
W-What?! Kourin is sick?!

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.690
Don't cry!

00:01:59.690 --> 00:02:01.790
What should I do?! Kourin's sick!

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:03.350
It's okay!

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:08.660
She's just exhausted from our hard schedule, 
so there's nothing to worry about!

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:12.320
It's just the two of us, but we'll 
do our best to cheer everyone on!

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:13.850
Thank you for your support.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:19.730
Why did it have to be Kourin?!

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.000
I'm worried!

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:25.310
Come to think of it, Miwa 
isn't here yet either...

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.040
Here we go.  Hold on tight!

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:33.710
Wait!

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:35.960
Kourin!

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:39.540
I wonder if something happened after that...

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:13.530
Okay!

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:17.390
The elimination block groupings, as 
chosen randomly by our computer, are...

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:19.600
...this!

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:25.770
Team Jurassic Army
 Team Q4
 Team Spyder

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:25.740
So we're in C Block...

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:30.170
We're with Jurassic Army, Team Spyder...

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:32.250
...and, um...

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:32.250
Team FFBS

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.020
FF...?

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:35.460
Foo Fighter?

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:38.910
What?! Ren Suzugamori's team?

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:41.260
That's too soon!

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:42.970
TS, yo!

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.060
Look carefully, everyone.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:47.010
If you're thinking of Ren's AL4...

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:49.660
Team Mermaid Angels
 Team FFAL4
 Team Furinkazan

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:49.640
...they're in F Block.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:53.850
Incidentally, Team Caesar is in A Block.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:57.300
The other powerful teams are 
all in other blocks, too.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:02.760
Shadow Paladin

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:07.040
Well, heck! Then C Block 
should be a piece of cake!

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.440
Big talk.

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:11.020
Who the heck are you people?

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:14.830
The team you were just gossiping about, FFBS.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:19.220
We're Team Foo Fighter Brilliant Stars.

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:21.960
And I'm the leader, Kiriya Bidou.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.940
I'm pleased to make your acquaintance.

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:28.780
Sorry. He didn't mean anything by it...

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:31.710
W-Well, I <i>was</i> a little too meager.

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:33.170
You mean <i>eager</i>.

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:36.630
"Brilly and Start"?

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:38.310
That's a weird name, huh?

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:40.800
He said "Brilliant Stars"!

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:43.030
You know, as in "Twinkle, Twinkle"...

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:44.900
Like twinkling stars...

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:45.670
Right!

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:50.770
We're beautiful stars, shining 
brightly in the night sky.

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:53.970
Compared to our elegant selves...

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:57.070
...even real stars grow dim.

00:05:57.070 --> 00:06:00.080
Oh, how sinful can we get?

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:03.100
Hey, looks like impressive opponents again!

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:04.420
And you look emaciated...

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:06.500
Show-offs!

00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:09.760
They make me itchy all over!

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:15.620
I was right after all! Apologies to Manager, 
but we're gonna clean your clocks!

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:19.020
After all, you guys are just 
AL4's substitute team, right?!

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:23.850
Substitutes? Hmm... That's 
not entirely incorrect...

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:29.010
...but do you know how many fighters 
are currently in Foo Fighter?

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:32.690
Huh? Why would I know something like that?

00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:35.240
Um... about 30?

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.930
Sorry, not even close. 
There are 500 fighters.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:39.580
F-Five hundred?!

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:44.140
All of those fighters train 
again and again, every day,

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:47.430
to get stronger and to 
climb to a higher position.

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:50.200
They do it to get even a little 
closer to Ren, you see.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:55.900
New teams are chosen from those who win 
that severe struggle for existence.

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:59.270
And that would be us, Brilliant Stars.

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:03.020
For your own sake, you shouldn't just 
think of us as a "substitute team".

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:10.290
So this is where you went, Bidou.

00:07:13.810 --> 00:07:15.450
Team Q4?

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:18.580
Although I don't see Kai...

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:22.260
I don't see Ren over there, either!

00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:24.280
What's wrong? Did he run away scared?

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:26.320
Of course he didn't!

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:28.480
Asaka, don't play his game.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:34.990
Ren wants to talk to you.

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:36.010
Understood.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:38.770
Well, I'll see you again soon...

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:40.650
...Team Q4...

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:43.980
...and Aichi Sendou.

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:45.470
Yes.

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:52.680
Why did that guy say your name, Brother?

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:55.680
Beats me. I'm looking forward 
to the fight, though, you know?

00:07:56.310 --> 00:07:56.910
Right!

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.750
You can leave.

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:10.440
Very well.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:17.680
What did you think of Aichi Sendou?

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:21.320
I can't tell from the few words we exchanged.

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:23.320
Is that right?

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:26.260
I think you didn't like him.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:29.310
There's no need to hide it.

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:34.030
You don't like that I gave Aichi Sendou 
that Shadow Paladin deck, do you?

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:38.740
Why?

00:08:39.020 --> 00:08:41.810
Why do you think so much of him?

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:45.250
It wouldn't be an overstatement 
to say it was Aichi Sendou's fault

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:48.130
that Q4 didn't make it to the 
finals in the last tournament!

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:52.010
You entrusted that deck to a guy like him?!

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:55.510
I'm counting on you, Bidou.

00:08:56.080 --> 00:09:01.220
Even without Shadow Paladin, you're more 
than able to do the job, aren't you?

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:03.730
Of course!

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:09.480
If you can prove your worth to me, 
the current vacant fourth position of AL4…

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:12.730
Yes. It'll be yours.

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:16.830
I'll do everything in my power 
to live up to your expectations.

00:09:23.530 --> 00:09:28.710
The stage is set. Show me the next 
step in the evolution of Psyqualia...

00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:31.120
...Aichi Sendou.

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:35.220
Kourin's still not here, huh?

00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:41.150
We've got fierce fights developing 
among the blocks at all the sites!

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:45.160
In A Block, one of the best bets for 
the championship, Team Caesar is...

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:48.410
Whoops! They've apparently won already.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:50.890
The winner is Kenji Mitsusada!

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:56.320
With a win-loss record of 2-0, Team 
Caesar has aced the first round!

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.850
Incidentally, this footage is a recording.

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:06.580
Team Caesar!

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:08.540
Hi! Long time no see.

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:10.800
You came to cheer us on, huh?

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:12.810
Well, something like that...

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:16.300
Congratulations on winning 
the first round... I presume?

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:20.310
Not like it's decided that we're 
going to the final round...

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:22.140
Um... Aichi?

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:23.390
Yes?

00:10:23.610 --> 00:10:26.640
Well? Have you put together a good deck now?

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:30.600
Yes. The ultimate deck.

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:34.110
Huh. That's what I call confidence...

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:37.120
The next teams, please get ready.

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:40.420
I repeat: the next teams, please get ready.

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:42.160
All right! We've gotta go!

00:10:42.610 --> 00:10:44.160
Well, good luck!

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:47.330
I look forward to fighting 
you guys in the finals.

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:49.190
"Good luck"?

00:10:51.780 --> 00:10:54.670
We're going to make it to the final round.

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:56.200
Whether you wish us luck or not.

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:00.610
Later!

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:08.670
He seems different somehow...

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:20.390
It's been a while, Aichi Sendou.

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:22.090
Yes, it has.

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:25.570
Fancy meeting you again in the first 
match of the elimination round.

00:11:25.570 --> 00:11:27.910
Looks to me like fate.

00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:30.900
Last time, victory was ours...

00:11:31.240 --> 00:11:34.170
...but how about now? Have 
you gotten any stronger?

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:36.870
Have you?

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:42.200
I'm a little fed up with that topic today.

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:42.940
What?

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:47.650
Everyone seems to think that I have 
not changed since the last encounter.

00:11:47.650 --> 00:11:53.190
Apparently, it's necessary to 
demonstrate that I've been reborn.

00:11:56.120 --> 00:11:59.900
I apologize in advance, but I'm 
going to wipe the floor with you.

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:03.730
It's only natural to do your best in a fight.

00:12:03.730 --> 00:12:06.060
But I like that spirit!

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:10.090
The gun signaling the beginning 
of the battle has fired!

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:19.310
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:12:26.210 --> 00:12:29.640
Fullbau? Then that means his deck is...

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:31.850
...Shadow Paladin?!

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:37.570
Why? He took such good care 
of that Royal Paladin deck...

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:59.710
The first and second fights of the 
elimination round are unfolding in these halls.

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:06.070
This hall hosts the battle between 
Q4 and the Jurassic Army!

00:13:06.070 --> 00:13:09.130
It's Aichi Sendou from Team Q4

00:13:09.130 --> 00:13:12.640
versus Gunji Ryuudou of the Jurassic Army!

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:16.110
A hot fight is developing as I speak!

00:13:17.110 --> 00:13:18.770
Go, Gigarex!

00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:23.740
No guard.

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:28.200
Damage trigger check.

00:13:29.920 --> 00:13:34.700
Uh oh! Now Aichi Sendou is up to 5 damage!

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:39.020
Still, Ryuudou doesn't have any 
more units that he can attack with.

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:44.170
My turn is over!

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:50.770
Sendou has skillfully hung in 
there after repeated attacks.

00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:54.460
Ryuudou, on the other 
hand, also has 5 damage...

00:13:54.860 --> 00:13:58.000
I have a feeling this next turn 
is going to be very hard on him.

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:02.980
Final Turn!

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:04.480
What?!

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:08.470
My goodness! Sendou has just 
announced his "final turn"!

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:09.870
Again?

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:11.200
Brother...

00:14:14.570 --> 00:14:16.250
I stand and draw.

00:14:17.950 --> 00:14:19.440
Cursed dragon,

00:14:19.890 --> 00:14:22.130
come out and muster your dark power!

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:23.820
I ride...

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:27.090
...Phantom Blaster Dragon!

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:35.080
I call Dark Mage, Badhabh Caar.

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:46.860
Badhabh Caar's skill...

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:49.110
I call Abyss Freezer.

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:53.110
And then...

00:14:53.800 --> 00:14:58.680
Yes. Unleash the power, Aichi...

00:14:59.130 --> 00:15:01.130
Phantom Blaster Dragon's...

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:02.610
...Counterblast!

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:05.550
Damned Charging Lance!

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:18.330
You sacrificed your own allies?!

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:24.040
When in command, sometimes it's 
necessary to be cold-hearted.

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:25.430
Yes, certainly...

00:15:25.430 --> 00:15:28.630
...but I never thought that you, of 
all people, would use that strategy!

00:15:28.950 --> 00:15:33.740
On top of that, I call Blaster Dark 
and Witch of Nostrum, Arianrhod!

00:15:35.790 --> 00:15:40.370
With a boost from Arianrhod... 
Go, Phantom Blaster Dragon!

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:42.880
Crush Deathrex!

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:51.260
I don't have enough cards!

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:53.760
No guard!

00:15:54.460 --> 00:15:55.850
Twin drive...

00:15:59.550 --> 00:16:01.500
All right! You didn't get a trigger, huh?

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:05.220
No. But 2 damage is certain.

00:16:05.220 --> 00:16:10.410
The only way out of this pinch for you 
is to draw 2 heal triggers in a row.

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:11.400
Indeed.

00:16:12.020 --> 00:16:15.300
This brings to mind our fight 
from last time, doesn't it?

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:21.370
I lost then... but I wonder 
how it'll turn out this time?

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:27.450
Damage trigger, first check!

00:16:28.860 --> 00:16:30.370
Heal trigger activated!

00:16:31.330 --> 00:16:32.960
He drew a trigger!

00:16:32.960 --> 00:16:33.880
I don't believe it!

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:37.770
Another nightmare?

00:16:37.770 --> 00:16:39.480
AN?!

00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:40.600
Aichi...

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:42.750
I'm not surprised...

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:45.100
...but what about the second card?

00:16:54.770 --> 00:16:58.020
Goddess of Battle, give me victory!

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:07.730
The winner is Aichi Sendou!

00:17:08.050 --> 00:17:09.970
The showdown is over!

00:17:09.970 --> 00:17:13.420
Team Q4 won the first match!

00:17:19.490 --> 00:17:21.480
Congratulations, Aichi.

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:23.130
But you've got a long ways to go.

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:27.160
That's not your true power.

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:34.400
This kid just keeps getting 
stronger, doesn't he?

00:17:34.770 --> 00:17:37.260
Yes. But...

00:17:37.260 --> 00:17:38.160
"But"?

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:46.080
My army has suffered a complete defeat.

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:48.160
You definitely have changed.

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:50.820
You're strong. You've gotten stronger!

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:56.170
Now do you understand what I 
meant when I said I was reborn?

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:04.580
But now, you're no longer worthy of a salute...

00:18:07.340 --> 00:18:09.170
You did it, Brother!

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:19.240
Aichi?!

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:21.660
Brother!

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:23.720
Brother!

00:18:23.260 --> 00:18:24.670
I'm strong...

00:18:25.020 --> 00:18:26.790
I've gotten stronger...

00:18:31.490 --> 00:18:32.840
Where am I?

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:39.760
Kai!

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:43.010
Wait! Kai!

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:45.080
Wait!

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:49.630
I-I've gotten stronger!

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:51.520
Kai!

00:18:56.840 --> 00:18:57.900
Kai...

00:19:15.120 --> 00:19:16.750
You're awake?

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:17.880
Emi...

00:19:18.150 --> 00:19:21.340
I see... I collapsed again...

00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:25.740
What about the fight?

00:19:26.760 --> 00:19:29.010
Right now, Kamui's up...

00:19:33.740 --> 00:19:37.190
Attack, Stern Blaukruger!

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:39.190
Stardust Shooting!

00:19:45.730 --> 00:19:47.900
Thanks to Kamui Katsuragi's 
ferocious attacks,

00:19:48.360 --> 00:19:50.700
Jurassic Army is defeated!

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:54.160
Chalk up a victory for Team Q4!

00:19:59.310 --> 00:20:00.340
Aichi...

00:20:02.110 --> 00:20:03.430
Thank you.

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:11.920
Yes! Their first victory!

00:20:11.920 --> 00:20:13.670
FV, yo!

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:16.660
Maybe we can get our hopes up this time...

00:20:16.660 --> 00:20:18.150
Right, Morikawa?

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:19.270
H-Huh?

00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:25.710
All of this Kourin merchandise is mine!

00:20:31.510 --> 00:20:32.660
Kourin?

00:20:35.850 --> 00:20:36.990
That <i>is</i> her!

00:20:37.720 --> 00:20:39.610
Kourin!

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:42.470
Kourin!

00:20:46.650 --> 00:20:48.850
Ah! Kourin's...!

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:51.480
Aah! Kourin's...!

00:20:52.470 --> 00:20:54.370
Kourin!!

00:20:58.200 --> 00:20:59.070
Yes?

00:21:00.770 --> 00:21:01.820
In here?

00:21:02.850 --> 00:21:05.140
It's okay. You can come in.

00:21:05.140 --> 00:21:07.320
Misaki, Kamui...

00:21:08.320 --> 00:21:10.490
Are you all right, Brother?

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:13.280
Yeah. I feel refreshed 
after taking a little nap.

00:21:13.280 --> 00:21:14.820
I'll be fine for my next fight...

00:21:16.700 --> 00:21:17.830
Huh?

00:21:18.070 --> 00:21:20.980
You're not ready yet, Aichi. 
You need to rest some more.

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:24.510
I'm fine, I tell you!

00:21:30.020 --> 00:21:31.230
Did you notice?

00:21:31.230 --> 00:21:36.310
Yeah. Brother is routinely 
weak after a fight.

00:21:37.140 --> 00:21:39.710
After the fight with 
Fragrance at regionals...

00:21:40.520 --> 00:21:42.700
And when he fought Kyou...

00:21:45.230 --> 00:21:47.950
I don't know why it happens...

00:21:47.980 --> 00:21:52.520
Infirmary

00:21:48.580 --> 00:21:51.940
...but we can't let Brother fight anymore.

00:21:52.710 --> 00:21:57.110
You and I will win the rest 
of the fights. Got it?

00:21:57.110 --> 00:21:58.280
Of course!

00:22:09.620 --> 00:22:13.220
Hurry up, Toshiki Kai.

00:23:50.580 --> 00:23:53.620
We can't let Aichi fight when he's like that.

00:23:53.620 --> 00:23:57.450
Yeah. Why always after a 
fight? Maybe he's exhausted?

00:23:57.450 --> 00:24:00.130
Anyway, the two of us will keep winning.

00:24:00.130 --> 00:24:02.530
That way, Aichi can get some rest.

00:24:02.530 --> 00:24:05.540
No problem! Misaki, you and I 
together are a winning machine!

00:24:05.540 --> 00:24:08.360
I'm touched that you two 
are worried about me...

00:24:08.360 --> 00:24:09.760
...but are you sure it's 
okay for me to rest up?

00:24:09.760 --> 00:24:11.700
Our next opponents may be tough, too.

00:24:11.700 --> 00:24:13.760
Next time: The Coiling Thread.

00:24:14.220 --> 00:24:16.550
I can't picture you two losing.

00:24:16.550 --> 00:24:17.870
I believe in you.
